Subject: [PATCH] Fix the two baseline regressions: anvil receipt race,
 rewritten registry fixture provenance

credit-vault-relay-concurrency: anvil answers a submission before its automined
block is sealed (measured: the transaction is already out of the pool and its
receipt appears ~20 ms later, mined once). The test read the receipt in that
window after the operator's rebroadcast (and once after the owner's deploy). It
now waits for the mined receipt at those two reads; every exactly-once
assertion (broadcast counts, signatures, payer nonce, balances, journal
"confirmed", same hash) is unchanged.

cli-independent / lease-gas-fixtures: the registry schema-4 fixture is the
published copy changed by the user-authorized 2026-10-21 history rewrite
(comment lines only). test/fixtures/registry-schema4/PROVENANCE.json ties it
(sha256 771a22d3, blob 3086cf42) to the manifest's pinned original (b17db9a3,
blob d7fb9740, sha256 e81f5d51), which is left unchanged. The test proves what
the published repository can: compiling the published file gives the deployed
executable bytes, and with the deployed CBOR metadata rebuilt from the
manifest's metadataIpfs the runtime hashes to the live codeHash 39911d6f; its
own metadata differs, so the rewritten text is never claimed as the deployed
source. No removed text is restored.
